{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788318334,"nonce":"XZIogBnzPfvKAU8HPHNnrVHbxUc=","title":"**From run `m1-20260901`'s post-mortem, cause C2** — the one output the ladder says is owed and that no existing artifact covers. It is a **deterministic** finding, so by `postmortem.md` step 5 it belongs in the mod regardless of which lower rung would also have \"worked\".","message":"Wouter went down at tick 244,343 and developed a wound infection. Over the next four in-game days it climbed **0.13 → 0.93**, with 1.0 the value that kills, and **nobody tended him** for roughly 8,000 ticks after the rescue put him in his own bed.\n\nThe reason: I had set **Lacey — the colony's only *available* doctor — to `Mining` priority 1** to break a steel bottleneck, four days earlier. Her `Doctor` sat at 2. Mining outranked Doctor on every think tick and she mined.\n\n**`digest.work_coverage.ok` read `true` for the entire period.** It was not lying. The Doctor row was satisfied on its own terms:\n\n```\n{\"work\":\"Doctor\",\"floor\":2,\"floor_on\":\"available\",\"have\":2,\n \"available_pawns\":[\"Wouter\",\"Lacey\"], ...}\n```\n\nTwo doctors, both enabled, both available. The floor is met. And no job was ever produced, because *enabled and available* is not the same as *reachable given what else that pawn was told to do first*.\n\n\nThe mistake is mine and the post-mortem says so. But the four-day invisibility is not: **nothing in the surface compares a work type's floor against the pawns' priority ranks.** `one-doctor-is-zero-doctors` graduated into code as an availability check (`40ed42f`), and this is the same lesson exactly one level down — a doctor who exists, is enabled, is awake, is not the patient, and is *outranked*.\n\nThe generalisation is worth stating because it is not specific to Doctor: **a floor satisfied only by pawns whose top priority lies elsewhere is a floor satisfied on paper.** The same shape will hide an uncovered Firefighter during a fire, or an uncovered Construction while the base burns down, and in every case `work_coverage.ok` will read true.\n\nNote that this is *not* the `who-will-actually-do-it` bill trap (`WorkGiver_DoBill.ShouldSkip`'s `billGiver != pawn`). That one is about eligibility. This one is about precedence, and the two can both be satisfied while nothing happens.\n\n\nEvery input is already published, on the same call:\n\n- `work_coverage.rows[].available_pawns` — who counts toward the floor\n- each pawn's `work.row[]` — `{work, priority}` for all 26 work types\n- `Find.PlaySettings.useWorkPriorities` — whether the numbers mean anything at all (with manual priorities off, `GetPriority` returns a flat 3 and this whole check is vacuous, which is itself worth reporting)\n\nNo simulation, no pathfinding, no tick. It is a comparison over two things the digest already holds — the same standard `work-cover` already meets when it picks a promotion in `Pawn_WorkSettings.EnableAndInitialize`'s own order.\n\n\n1. `work_coverage`'s rows gain a precedence reading per counted pawn: that pawn's priority for **this** work type, and its best (numerically lowest) priority across all work types. Proposed field names `priority` and `top_priority`, alongside the existing `available_pawns`.\n2. A row whose floor is met **only** by pawns that are outranked reports it — a distinct verdict, not a silent `ok`. Proposed: keep `ok` for the floor arithmetic and add `outranked: [{pawn, work_priority, top_priority, top_work}]` plus a roll-up flag so a caller can branch without walking the list. **Do not repurpose `ok`**: the floor genuinely IS met and a run that trusted `ok` to mean \"the floor is met\" should not silently change meaning.\n3. It reports honestly when priorities are off: with `useWorkPriorities` false, every active type is a flat 3, so the check cannot fire and must say so rather than returning an empty list that reads like \"all clear\".\n4. `work-cover` grows a matching repair: promote the work type's priority on an available pawn to at or above its best, journalled as an act with the before/after — the same shape as its existing enable-and-initialise promotion. A `still_under`-equivalent when the roster genuinely cannot answer.\n5. `checklists/triggered.md §roster-change` and `daily.md`'s coverage reading cite it, so the check surfaces at the moment it bites — a lesson no checklist cites is half-landed.\n6. `accept/\u003cid\u003e-work-rank.py` on a bench: two doctors, one of them the patient's only hope, set the other's Mining to 1 and Doctor to 2, assert `ok` stays true AND the new field names her, assert `work-cover` repairs it, assert the priorities-off case reports vacuity rather than silence.\n\n\nReproduced exactly by run `m1-20260901`: `work-priorities {set:[{pawn:310, works:[\"Mining\"], priority:1}]}` while pawn 310 was one of two `available_pawns` on the Doctor row, patient 313 downed and untended, `tend_quality` 0.38 when tending finally started, infection severity 0.93 at its peak.","files":null}]}